---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Uses" description="The tools Aditya uses to write and make things.">
  <article class="standalone prose">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Uses</p>
      <h1>Tools I reach for.</h1>
      <p>A short list of dependable tools, not an endorsement catalogue.</p>
    </header>
    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Plain-text Markdown for notes that should outlive any one app.</li>
      <li>A paper notebook for thinking before a screen asks for speed.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Making for the web</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Astro for content that should ship as clear, static HTML.</li>
      <li>TypeScript for making assumptions explicit.</li>
      <li>Plain CSS for small, understandable interfaces.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Principle</h2>
    <p>I prefer tools with legible formats, excellent defaults, and an easy exit. The tool should make the work quieter, not become the work.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
